# Documentation Requirements
Rule Type: Always

## Required Documentation
### Project Documentation
- README.md with setup instructions
- API documentation for all public methods
- Trading strategy documentation
- Configuration guide
- Deployment guide

### Code Documentation
- Google style docstrings
- Type hints for all functions
- Parameter documentation
- Return value documentation
- Usage examples

## Documentation Format
### Docstring Requirements
- Use Google style docstrings
- Include type hints
- Document all parameters
- Document return values
- Include usage examples

### Code Comments
- Explain complex logic
- Document assumptions
- Note limitations
- Include TODOs
- Reference related code

## Strategy Documentation
### Required Sections
- Strategy overview
- Entry/exit logic
- Risk management
- Performance metrics
- Usage examples

### Technical Details
- Indicator calculations
- Signal generation
- Position sizing
- Error handling
- Performance considerations

## API Documentation
### Method Documentation
- Purpose and usage
- Parameters and types
- Return values
- Exceptions
- Examples

### Class Documentation
- Class purpose
- Attributes
- Methods
- Usage examples
- Inheritance

## Configuration Documentation
### Required Sections
- Environment setup
- Configuration parameters
- Trading parameters
- Risk parameters
- System settings

### Usage Guide
- Installation steps
- Configuration steps
- Running instructions
- Troubleshooting
- Best practices

## Maintenance Requirements
### Documentation Updates
- Update with code changes
- Review regularly
- Version control
- Change tracking
- Quality checks

### Documentation Review
- Technical accuracy
- Completeness
- Clarity
- Examples
- Formatting

## Version Control
### Documentation Versioning
- Match code versions
- Track changes
- Maintain history
- Update changelog
- Tag releases

### Change Management
- Document all changes
- Update affected docs
- Review changes
- Track updates
- Maintain consistency
